 {id:'transfer-detail-2',skill:'細節理解',story:'Mia will meet her cousin at the south gate of the park at ten. Her cousin first suggested the east gate, but it is closed for repairs. Mia will bring water, and her cousin will bring lunch.',prompt:'Where will they meet?',options:['At the east gate.','Inside a restaurant.','At the south gate.','At the train station.'],answer:2,evidence:'Mia will meet her cousin at the south gate of the park at ten.',explanation:'要分辨最初提議和最後約定；東門已關閉。',reasons:['東門是最初提議，因維修而未採用。','文章未提到餐廳。','第一句明確指定南門。','文章未提到車站。']},
 {id:'transfer-inference-1',skill:'推論判讀',story:'Before leaving home, Jack saw dark clouds. He put an umbrella in his bag, although the road was still dry. Later, his classmates ran into school with wet hair. Jack arrived with dry hair.',prompt:'Why did Jack probably stay dry?',options:['He stayed at home all day.','He likely used his umbrella.','His classmates washed his hair.','It did not rain anywhere.'],answer:1,evidence:'He put an umbrella in his bag, although the road was still dry.',explanation:'結合帶傘、同學頭髮濕、Jack 頭髮乾三個線索，可推測他用傘遮雨。這是推論，不是原文明說。',reasons:['最後一句說他到校了。','帶傘和乾髮的線索支持這個推論。','原文沒有洗頭的行為。','烏雲與同學濕髮不支持這個解釋。']},
 {id:'transfer-inference-2',skill:'推論判讀',story:'Lily practiced her speech in front of her little brother. Whenever he looked confused, she replaced a difficult word with an easier one. The next day, her class could follow her talk without asking what the words meant.',prompt:'Why did Lily change some words?',options:['To make her speech longer.','To hide the topic from her class.','To avoid practicing again.','To make her ideas easier to understand.'],answer:3,evidence:'Whenever he looked confused, she replaced a difficult word with an easier one.',explanation:'弟弟困惑時才換簡單字，後來同學也聽懂，支持「讓內容易懂」的目的。',reasons:['沒有增加長度的線索。','換簡單字是幫助理解，並非隱藏主題。','她正在練習，沒有說要逃避練習。','困惑、簡化字詞、聽懂三個線索一致。']},
 {id:'transfer-word-1',skill:'字義推測',story:'The bus was packed. Every seat was taken, and many people had to stand. Ben waited for the next bus because he wanted more space.',prompt:'What does “packed” mean here?',options:['Full of people.','Put inside a box.','Broken and empty.','Moving very slowly.'],answer:0,evidence:'Every seat was taken, and many people had to stand.',explanation:'每個座位都有人，還有人站著，因此 packed 在這裡指擁擠、擠滿人。',reasons:['座位滿了和站客很多支持此義。','不是在描述裝箱。','有人坐、有人站，並非空車。','原文未描述車速。']},
 {id:'transfer-word-2',skill:'字義推測',story:'Please keep your voice low in this room. Several students are taking a test, and loud talking may disturb them.',prompt:'What does “disturb” mean here?',options:['Give a useful gift to.','Help someone finish faster.','Make it hard for someone to concentrate.','Invite someone to a party.'],answer:2,evidence:'Several students are taking a test, and loud talking may disturb them.',explanation:'考試需要專心，因此大聲說話會干擾他們。',reasons:['文中沒有送禮。','大聲說話不被描述成幫助。','考試和降低音量的語境支持「干擾」。','文中沒有聚會邀請。']},
 {id:'transfer-main-1',skill:'主旨統整',story:'Our class used to throw away paper with only one side used. Now we keep it in a box near the printer. We use the blank sides for notes and drawings. This simple change helps us buy less paper.',prompt:'What is the best title?',options:['How to Buy a New Printer','Giving Used Paper Another Job','Why Drawing Is Difficult','The Biggest Box in School'],answer:1,evidence:'We use the blank sides for notes and drawings.',explanation:'全篇描述把單面廢紙收集並再利用，主旨應涵蓋這個改變。',reasons:['沒有購買印表機的過程。','涵蓋收集、再用與減少購紙的內容。','畫圖只是用途之一，文章沒說很難。','箱子只是工具，大小不是重點。']},
 {id:'transfer-main-2',skill:'主旨統整',story:'Tom tried to learn twenty new words in one evening and forgot most of them. He then studied five words a day and reviewed older ones each morning. After two weeks, he could use more words in his writing.',prompt:'What is the main idea?',options:['Learning is only useful at night.','Writing requires exactly twenty words.','Old words should never be reviewed.','Small amounts of study with review can help learning.'],answer:3,evidence:'He then studied five words a day and reviewed older ones each morning.',explanation:'前後比較大量一次學與少量持續複習；後者讓 Tom 更能運用單字。',reasons:['新的方法包含早晨複習。','二十是最初學習量，不是作文規則。','文章中的進步包含複習舊字。','同時涵蓋少量學習、複習與進步。']},
 {id:'transfer-integrate-1',skill:'資訊整合',story:'Museum tickets cost $100 for adults and $60 for students. On Sundays, every visitor pays half price. The discount does not apply to the $20 audio guide. Amy is a student and visits on Sunday without an audio guide.',prompt:'How much does Amy pay?',options:['$30.','$50.','$60.','$80.'],answer:0,evidence:'On Sundays, every visitor pays half price.',explanation:'Amy 是學生，票價 60 元；週日半價為 30 元，且她不租導覽機。',reasons:['學生 60 元乘以一半，得到 30 元。','50 元是成人半價，或錯加導覽機。','60 元是未打折學生票。','80 元忽略折扣且多算導覽機。']},
 {id:'transfer-integrate-2',skill:'資訊整合',story:'The cooking class runs from 9:00 to 10:30. The art class runs from 10:00 to 11:00. The music class runs from 11:30 to 12:30. Sara is free from 10:45 until 13:00 and wants to attend a whole class.',prompt:'Which class can Sara attend from start to finish?',options:['Only cooking.','Only art.','Only music.','Both cooking and art.'],answer:2,evidence:'Sara is free from 10:45 until 13:00 and wants to attend a whole class.',explanation:'完整課程要在 10:45 後開始、13:00 前結束，只有音樂課符合。',reasons:['烹飪課 9:00 開始，早於她有空的時間。','美術課 10:00 開始，她會錯過前 45 分鐘。','11:30–12:30 全部落在她有空的區間。','兩堂都在她有空前開始。']}
